    description:
      "On July 22, 2026, the Central Bank of Jordan (CBJ) posted a public warning on its official Facebook page cautioning citizens about fraudulent advertisements circulating on social media that falsely tell users they have won a cash prize. The ads are built to capitalize on the excitement of an unexpected windfall, prompting people who click through to hand over personal and financial details that the CBJ said should never be shared with an unverified party regardless of what a message promises. \"Protecting your data starts with not sharing it with any untrusted party,\" the bank said in its warning, adding that no one should disclose banking information, national ID numbers, or other personal data to anyone claiming they have won a prize through a social media ad or message. The warning is part of a broader pattern of CBJ alerts about unlicensed entities and fraudulent offers circulating on social media in Jordan, and it reflects a scam format used worldwide: a bank, government agency, or well-known company never asks a winner to provide payment details, banking passwords, or personal identification numbers to claim a prize they never entered to win, and any message that does should be treated as fraudulent and reported rather than answered.",
