    slug: 'chad-fake-finance-ministry-crypto-scam',
    description: `Chad's Ministry of Finance, Budget, Economy, Planning and International Cooperation published a formal public denial on July 19, 2025 after a fraudulent document began circulating on WhatsApp and social media under the ministry's old name and the signature of a former state minister. The fake "note d'information" presented a fictitious cryptocurrency investment opportunity as though it were an official government program, and was designed to pressure recipients into handing over identification documents and other personal or financial information. The ministry stated the circular did not originate from it and that it had never authorized any cryptocurrency investment scheme, stressing that its genuine communications are issued only through official press releases, its institutional website, and its certified social-media accounts. It urged citizens to refuse sharing identification or financial details in response to any unsolicited message claiming to be from the ministry, to verify any purported government notice through official channels before acting on it, and to report anyone who receives or is targeted by the fraudulent document to the relevant authorities.`,
    categorySlug: 'government-impersonation',
